# Gate step 1302-7j8p — data, not code.
#
# Binds the checker that keeps a gate step from entering --check on one
# regime's word. Source-text only: it reads STEP_SECOND_REGIME out of every
# .step file and never runs a step, so it needs no toolbox, no ruby and no
# guest, and it costs milliseconds.
#
# THIS STEP RECORDS ITS OWN SECOND-REGIME RUN, which is the point rather than a
# formality: a rule whose own enforcer is exempt teaches that the rule is for
# other people. The record below is the fixture's verdict on macneo, not the
# checker's verdict on the live tree — the fixture is what the regime needs
# (the checker's own output depends on how far the fleet's backfill has got,
# and would go stale the moment another step is recorded).
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking every gate step carries a recorded second-regime run (1302-7j8p)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/check-gate-step-regimes.sh"
STEP_ERROR="a gate step carries no recorded second-regime run (1302-7j8p) — it would enter the gate on one regime's word, which reddened both macOS gates twice in one day on 2026-09-20; add STEP_SECOND_REGIME to the named step, and a named skip counts"
STEP_OK="every gate step carries a second-regime record"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:gate-step-regimes-fixture:4/4"
